  "problem": "HCRIS facility/report/year and PLACES county/measure/year could collapse into a generic hospital or person tag. Undocumented dimensions could be inferred. A metadata-modified date could fill observation end. A projection to 2100 could be treated as observed future data. Overlapping ACS periods and rolling releases could be flattened. Incompatible fiscal and calendar years could be treated as equivalent. Editing sealed identity researcher-guidance or normalization src would break WP7/normalization artifact seals.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Grain and time live in packages/enrichment/grain-and-time.mjs. Observation grain, sampled entity, reporting organization, universe and geographic dimension are separate evidenced fields with explicit unknown states. HCRIS facility/report/year and PLACES county/measure/year cannot collapse into generic hospital/person tags. Date roles bind only from captured statements. A metadata-modified date cannot fill observation end. A projection to 2100 is not observed future data. Overlapping ACS periods and rolling releases are preserved. Incompatible reporting periods yield INCOMPATIBLE_REPORTING_PERIODS; there is no automatic fiscal-to-calendar equivalence. Source-native terms remain visible alongside normalized fields. Sealed packages/identity/src and packages/normalization/src are unchanged.",
